// transport that signs the body signs those octets. The caller owns everything
// about the transport itself: auth headers, X-Signature over req.body, and
// status handling beyond "2xx parses, the rest throws ApiError" — a 401
// policy, retries. A client has no persistence and no cache of its own.
//
