// entry points exist so a consumer of only the public surface does not acquire
// the authenticated routes. The envelope below — Transport, ClientRequest,
// ClientResponse and ApiError — is shared by all of them on purpose: two
// ApiError classes would make `instanceof` depend on which entry point the
// catch block imported from, which is silent and wrong in one direction.

